<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rani of Jhansi Regiment</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmibai">Rani of Jhansi</a> Regiment was the women's regiment of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-army">Indian National Army</a>, formed in 1943 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subhas-chandra-bose">Subhas Chandra Bose</a> and commanded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmi">Lakshmi</a> Swaminathan, later Lakshmi Sahgal. Named after Rani Lakshmibai of Jhansi, a leader of the rebellion of 1857, it recruited mainly among Indian women in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>. Part of it served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> before it was disbanded in 1945.</p></div>
